meta {
  name: 11 - Home Polling Debug
  seq: 11
}

docs {
  Requests for debugging the reduced Home polling flow under local-firebase.

  Use these to compare:
  - GET /api/me/home/status: cheap persisted version + dirty flag.
  - GET /api/me/home/pending: lightweight actionable state, no partner summaries.
  - GET /api/me/home: full Home source of truth.

  Android/current-user requests use firebase_id_token.
  Counterpart requests use firebase_counterpart_id_token.

  Typical Android debug flow:
  1. Run 00-02 here to sign in/provision the Android Firebase user.
  2. Use the app to perform the action under test.
  3. Run 10-12 here to compare status, pending and full Home.

  For counterpart-driven states, first run the setup part of
  "07 - Android First Chat Visual Counterpart" through request 12 to create,
  provision, profile, enqueue and match the counterpart against the Android user.
  Then run 20-22 here if the counterpart token needs refresh, and 30-32 to compare
  counterpart status, pending and full Home.
}
